  "description": "v2 (2026-09-15, main d1cbbf5d): the read lane now also carries the voice conversation-list pipeline (voice_conversation_list_cli.mjs, prompts/voice_conversation_list/) and the voice route CLI, and the read CLI answers --voice-session --conversation-list --corrections. The lane the context bot's skill calls to read: guild_hall/context_engine/harness/estate_graph_query.mjs finds an item and guild_hall/context_engine/harness/estate_original_read.mjs reads that item back to its original, including the attachment list and one attachment's text or page images. No scheduled task runs this lane — it is called per question, which is why it is separate from graph-sync-v1 (the 30-minute writer) rather than folded into it: a read lane can be rebuilt without touching the lane that is holding a lease. tracked_paths are the context engine plus exactly the dependency files its own runtime closure records, the same set graph-sync-v1 carries, so the two lanes stay byte-comparable where they overlap. There are no carried_forward_prefixes: every module imports node: builtins only.",
